WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.320
- So, speaking of looking great,

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:02.153
y'all look so great in that.

00:00:02.153 --> 00:00:03.750
So on your recent press tour,

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:05.610
you said that you didn't feel comfortable

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.200
wearing natural hairstyles

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.033
while in the White House.

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:09.780
So what exactly do you mean by that?

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.940
- You know, a lot of
people don't remember,

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.240
as the first black family
in the White House,

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.060
the, the journey there wasn't smooth.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.830
There were people who tried to-

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:20.663
- I Remember the news.

00:00:20.663 --> 00:00:22.980
Yeah.
- Turn us into others.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:24.900
- Yeah, division.
- And so,

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.730
we had to overcome a lot of that.

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:31.260
And so much was read into
gestures we would make,

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.750
like a fist bump was turned into a

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:36.030
terrorist fish jab.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.580
And so I was like, braids,

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.860
people aren't gonna understand braids.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.110
Sadly. Not at least at that time.

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:46.020
And I didn't want that
to be a distraction.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.880
There was too much to do.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:48.861
There was healthcare to-
- You didn't want to

00:00:48.861 --> 00:00:51.180
distract from the focus.
- Right.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.720
Now, fortunately, the, more people

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.880
are showing what it means to be beautiful,

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.140
what hair can look like.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.000
I'm grateful to this generation

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.935
that is owning every part of themselves.

00:01:01.935 --> 00:01:02.940
(audience claps)
- Absolutely.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.260
- So, now-
- A very bold generation.

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:06.720
And it's good.
- And, and we need it.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:08.010
- Yeah.
- 'Cause we need to

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:10.650
create a broader definition
of who's American,

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:13.020
who counts, what beauty is.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.210
It only helps our kids, who are,

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:17.370
we don't know who they're gonna become.

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:19.440
And we wanna make sure
there's a space for them

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:20.460
whoever they choose to be.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:22.110
- Why limit them? Yeah.

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:23.610
I think it, it should be celebrated.

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:24.443
And I think you're right.

00:01:24.443 --> 00:01:25.570
This younger generation
is very much into that.

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:28.020
- Yeah. And it shouldn't be politicized.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.160
- Yeah.
- Most kids who are

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.140
wearing tattoos and piercings,

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:32.430
they've got long nails.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:36.000
It's not about their, their value system.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.650
is about individuality.

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:38.483
- But back in the day,

00:01:38.483 --> 00:01:39.984
tattoos was like so bad.

00:01:39.984 --> 00:01:41.880
- It, well, and-
- And I came home with one,

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.087
and my mom just kind of
looked at it and was like,

00:01:43.087 --> 00:01:44.072
"That's new."

00:01:44.072 --> 00:01:45.360
(everyone laughs)
- Well, it was the same thing.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:47.490
My generation didn't,

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:50.130
we didn't, tattoos meant
something totally different.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:50.963
- [Kelly] I know.
- We used to

00:01:50.963 --> 00:01:52.980
threaten our kids that
if you get a tattoo,

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:55.020
we're gonna get exactly the same kind

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.621
and show it on TikTok or whatever.

00:01:56.621 --> 00:01:58.260
(Kelly laughs)
- Take the cool away.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.240
- Take the cool all away.
(Kelly laughs hysterically)

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.003
- That's a good parenting skill.

00:02:02.003 --> 00:02:05.280
- Just like we're gonna make it so uncool.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.826
Barack Obama's gonna have
a heart on his shoulder.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:07.998
(Kelly laughs hysterically)

00:02:07.998 --> 00:02:10.416
(audience applauds)
(Kelly laughs hysterically)

00:02:10.416 --> 00:02:13.623
- That was the greatest
mom tip of the day.

